# install.sh refuses these placeholders; pass --owners
# Reviewers are requested automatically; branch protection must require a code-owner review.
# Auth and data-model paths name a second owner (the security owner), so the PR needs a
# reviewer who is not the author plus the person who owns that risk.
*                        @your-org/reviewers
**/auth/**               @your-org/reviewers @your-org/security-owner
**/models/**             @your-org/reviewers @your-org/security-owner
**/migrations/**         @your-org/reviewers @your-org/security-owner
alembic/**               @your-org/reviewers @your-org/security-owner
.claude/**               @your-org/reviewers
.mcp.json                @your-org/security-owner
CLAUDE.md                @your-org/reviewers
scripts/**               @your-org/reviewers
.github/**               @your-org/reviewers
.devcontainer/**         @your-org/security-owner
docker-compose*.yml      @your-org/security-owner
compose*.yml             @your-org/security-owner
Dockerfile*              @your-org/security-owner
